### Vendor-Specific (Flag Always)

| Source Feature | Action |
|---|---|
| Oracle `ROWID`/`UROWID` | Refactor app — no portable equivalent |
| Oracle nested tables / VARRAY | Normalize into child table or `JSONB` |
| SQL Server `HIERARCHYID` | Refactor with `ltree` (PG) or recursive CTE |
| SQL Server `ROWVERSION` | PG `xmin` system column or trigger-maintained `BIGINT` |
| SQL Server `SQL_VARIANT` | Refactor — typed columns or `JSONB` |
| MySQL `ENUM` | Target `ENUM` (PG) or lookup table |
| MySQL `SET` | Normalize or array column |
| MySQL `YEAR` | `SMALLINT` + CHECK |
| PG `INET`/`CIDR`/`MACADDR` | Store as `VARCHAR` on others; validate at app layer |
| PG `RANGE` types | Decompose into `from`/`to` columns |
| Mongo `ObjectId` | `UUID` (preferred) or `CHAR(24)` |
| Mongo nested doc | Child table OR `JSONB` |
| DynamoDB PK+SK | Composite primary key in RDBMS |

### Precision / Encoding Cautions

- **NUMERIC unbounded** (PostgreSQL) — slower than fixed-precision; only use when needed.
- **DOUBLE** is not exact — never use for currency.
- **VARCHAR(n) byte vs char** — Oracle defaults to bytes; PG to characters; verify.
- **CHAR padding** differs — PG pads to length; many drivers trim on read.
- **Time precision**: SQL Server `DATETIME` ≈ 3.33 ms; `DATETIME2(7)` is 100 ns; PG `TIMESTAMP` is microseconds. Align target precision.
- Standardize on **UTF-8** at cluster level. MySQL: `utf8mb4` not `utf8` (3-byte). Oracle: `NLS_CHARACTERSET = AL32UTF8`.

